From: FP3 camera work
Subject: [PATCH] camera: refocus before a full-resolution capture

Taking a picture switches the source to the capture resolution - a
different sensor mode reached by restarting the pipeline - and the focus
the preview had settled on does not carry across that switch, so every
full-resolution shot came out soft. Refocus in the capture mode before
the shutter, the way the flash path already does under its light, but for
the ordinary no-flash shot too. Only when the camera focuses for itself;
a manual focus is the user's to keep.
--- a/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
+++ b/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
@@ -803,6 +803,15 @@
     /// How many 100 ms waits to allow the pipeline for coming back up after
     /// switching resolution for a picture.
     const CAPTURE_WAIT_TRIES: u32 = 50;
+    /// How long to let a refocus settle after the source switches to the
+    /// capture resolution, before the shutter runs.
+    ///
+    /// The switch restarts the pipeline in a different sensor mode, and the
+    /// focus the preview settled on does not carry across it, so the shot
+    /// refocuses first. There is no completion signal from the simple
+    /// pipeline, so the wait is a fixed one, long enough for its contrast
+    /// sweep on this hardware - the same figure the flash path already uses.
+    const CAPTURE_FOCUS_SETTLE_MS: u64 = 900;
 
     /// Creates a new [`Viewfinder`][crate::Viewfinder]
     ///
@@ -920,6 +929,22 @@
             log::warn!("Pipeline did not come back up before the capture");
         }
 
+        // The source has just switched to the capture resolution: a different
+        // sensor mode, reached by restarting the pipeline. The focus the
+        // preview held is not carried across that switch, so a shot fired now
+        // comes out at whatever the lens fell back to - which is why every
+        // full-resolution picture was soft. Refocus in the capture mode before
+        // the shutter, the way the flash path already does under its light.
+        // Only when the camera focuses for itself: a manual focus is the
+        // user's to keep.
+        if self.autofocus() {
+            self.trigger_autofocus();
+            glib::timeout_future(std::time::Duration::from_millis(
+                Self::CAPTURE_FOCUS_SETTLE_MS,
+            ))
+            .await;
+        }
+
         camerabin.emit_by_name::<()>("start-capture", &[]);
     }
 
